course: dictionary
lesson: 15197
title: A seer is someone who sees
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seer is a person who is believed to be able to see what will happen in the future. «The villagers climbed the hill to ask the ancient seer what the harvest would bring.» People climb up to ask about the future, so the clue tells you a seer knows what is coming.
explain: Seer is an old word for a prophet, and you may meet it in the Bible: «Samuel is called a seer in the Bible.» Seer comes from the word see, so a seer is literally someone who sees. Look for clues about seeing, knowing or telling the future.
explain: Be careful when you read myths and fantasy stories. «The seer foretold a great storm, so the sailors stayed in port.» Foretold means said before it happened, so the sailors stayed safe because of the warning. Real scientists say no one can truly see the future; forecasts use evidence instead.
fact: A seer is a person who is believed to be able to see what will happen in the future.
fact: A seer is another word for a prophet.
fact: In the Bible, Samuel is called a seer, which is an old word for a prophet.
fact: In myths and history, people visited seers such as the Oracle of Delphi in ancient Greece to ask about the future.
fact: Scientists say no one can truly see the future; weather forecasts use evidence instead.
exercise: «The villagers asked the ancient seer what the harvest would bring.» What is a seer? | A king who rules a village | *A person believed to be able to see what will happen in the future | A farmer who grows the harvest
exercise: «In the Bible, Samuel is called a seer.» Which word means the same as seer? | Harvest | Sailor | Greece | *Prophet
exercise: «The seer foretold a great storm, so the sailors stayed in port.» What does foretold mean? | *Said what would happen before it happened | Sailed away quickly | Forgot the storm | Stayed very quiet
test: Scientists say no one can truly see the future. How do weather forecasts work instead? | They use magic from the sky | *They use evidence | They guess with their eyes closed | They ask a seer for help
test: Literally, what does seer mean in its simplest form? | Someone who runs fast | Someone who cooks | *Someone who sees | Someone who sings
exam: «The villagers climbed the hill to ask the seer about their future.» What is the best meaning of seer here? | A soldier who guards the village | *A person believed to be able to see the future | A teacher who tells stories | A farmer who grows crops
